          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You were in a road traffic collision. You had several injuries:\n\n- A broken left shin bone (tibia)\n- A small tear to your spleen\n- Broken ribs on the left side (ribs 7 to 9) with a small collection of blood around your lung\n- Small fractures to a bone in your lower back (L1)"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "We did scans to check all your injuries. Your spleen and blood levels were monitored closely and stayed stable. The spleen injury was treated without an operation.\n\nA drain was put into your chest to clear the blood around your lung. Scans and X-rays showed your lung was re-expanding well. The drain was removed on 15/05.\n\nOn 13/05, you had an operation on your left shin bone. A metal nail was placed inside the bone to hold it in place.\n\nThe physiotherapy team helped you start moving. You are putting some weight through your left leg, as guided by the bone specialists."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7"
          ],
          "text": "You have the following follow-up appointments:\n\n- Bone clinic (orthopaedics) in 2 weeks.\n- A phone call from the general surgery team about your spleen at 6 weeks. They will also give you advice about a vaccination related to your spleen injury.\n- The chest team do not need to see you for a routine appointment."
        },
